From 5114cd51792f7833f976c2b6e46533e3d34aa04b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 17:30:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 56/59] net: add the minimal telnet server for the rescue page
 (task-97)

The upstream web failsafe exposes a telnet server next to the HTTP
page.  Add a minimal RFC-854 server for the E2631 rescue image: one
connection at a time, IAC option negotiation (ECHO/SGA), line editing
with backspace and Ctrl-U, a 256-byte command line, and command
execution through the shared single slot so the web console and telnet
cannot run commands at the same time.

Output capture spans console record: the server swaps gd->console_out
for a private membuf around run_command(), drains it after the command
with CRLF normalisation and streams it back through the existing TCP
callback.  Ctrl-C during a command raises mtk_tcp_abort_request();
net_loop() now calls mtk_tcp_periodic_check() and consumes the pending
abort with the same cleanup as the serial Ctrl-C path.

The server listens on the telnet_port environment value, default 23,
and is started by e2631rescue next to the DHCP and DNS helpers.

Signed-off-by: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
